op:2px;\">Blended (credibility-weighted)<\/div>\n  <\/div>\n  <div style=\"flex:1; min-width:200px; background:#fff; border-top:4px solid #E74C3C; border-radius:6px; padding:14px 16px; box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.08);\">\n    <div style=\"font-size:.8em; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.04em; color:#7F8C8D;\">Chain Ladder reserve<\/div>\n    <div style=\"font-size:1.6em; font-weight:700; color:#E74C3C;\">25,536,718<\/div>\n    <div style=\"font-size:.85em; color:#566573; margin-top:2px;\">Std. error +/- n/a<\/div>\n  <\/div>\n  <div style=\"flex:1; min-width:200px; background:#fff; border-top:4px solid #16A085; border-radius:6px; padding:14px 16px; box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.08);\">\n    <div style=\"font-size:.8em; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.04em; color:#7F8C8D;\">Blend vs CL<\/div>\n    <div style=\"font-size:1.6em; font-weight:700; color:#16A085;\">-11,262,438<\/div>\n    <div style=\"font-size:.85em; color:#566573; margin-top:2px;\">Effect of stabilising green periods<\/div>\n  <\/div>\n  <div style=\"flex:1; min-width:200px; background:#fff; border-top:4px solid #B03A2E; border-radius:6px; padding:14px 16px; box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.08);\">\n    <div style=\"font-size:.8em; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.04em; color:#7F8C8D;\">Booked (after adjustments)<\/div>\n    <div style=\"font-size:1.6em; font-weight:700; color:#B03A2E;\">16,127,802<\/div>\n    <div style=\"font-size:.85em; color:#566573; margin-top:2px;\">Judgemental overlay +1,853,522 vs recommended<\/div>\n  <\/div>\n<\/div>\n<h5 style=\"margin-top:6px; color:#2C3E50;\">Key points for the decision<\/h5>\n<div style=\"border-left:4px solid #2C3E50; background:#F8F9FA; padding:10px 14px; margin-bottom:10px; border-radius:4px;\">\n  <div style=\"font-weight:600; color:#2C3E50; margin-bottom:2px;\">1. The number to book<\/div>\n  <div style=\"color:#34495E;\">Hold roughly <b>14,274,280<\/b> in IBNR reserves on this basis. This is the Blended (credibility-weighted) estimate, which keeps standard Chain Ladder for mature periods but anchors the newest, most volatile periods to a stable prior. Plain Chain Ladder alone gives <b>25,536,718<\/b> (a reduction of 11,262,438).<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<div style=\"border-left:4px solid #E67E22; background:#F8F9FA; padding:10px 14px; margin-bottom:10px; border-radius:4px;\">\n  <div style=\"font-weight:600; color:#2C3E50; margin-bottom:2px;\">2. Why we don't just use Chain Ladder<\/div>\n  <div style=\"color:#34495E;\">Chain Ladder is dependable for older periods but unstable for the newest ones, because it scales a tiny, noisy latest figure up by the full remaining development pattern. The least-developed periods here are <b>2023-12-01 (22% developed), 2023-11-01 (52% developed), 2023-10-01 (71% developed)<\/b>. These carry most of the estimate's uncertainty and are where the blend does its work; treat their raw CL numbers with caution.<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<div style=\"border-left:4px solid #F39C12; background:#F8F9FA; padding:10px 14px; margin-bottom:10px; border-radius:4px;\">\n  <div style=\"font-weight:600; color:#2C3E50; margin-bottom:2px;\">4. How much to trust the model<\/div>\n  <div style=\"color:#34495E;\">Back-testing on recently held-back data shows <b>reasonable<\/b> reliability (average error 10.9%, and a net bias of 7.0% versus actuals). The model tracks recent actuals acceptably; the headline numbers are usable with normal review.<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<div style=\"border-left:4px solid #2C3E50; background:#F8F9FA; padding:10px 14px; margin-bottom:10px; border-radius:4px;\">\n  <div style=\"font-weight:600; color:#2C3E50; margin-bottom:2px;\">5. Timing / cash-flow consideration<\/div>\n  <div style=\"color:#34495E;\">Payments peak in Dec (index 181) and trough in Aug (index 83) - a 97-point swing around the average.<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<div style=\"border-left:4px solid #E74C3C; background:#F8F9FA; padding:10px 14px; margin-bottom:10px; border-radius:4px;\">\n  <div style=\"font-weight:600; color:#2C3E50; margin-bottom:2px;\">6. Method agreement<\/div>\n  <div style=\"color:#34495E;\">Across all methods tried, total IBNR ranges over about <b>23,150,517<\/b> (roughly 162.2% of the recommended figure). The methods disagree materially - the final number is sensitive to method choice and warrants explicit sign-off.<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<div style=\"font-size:.8em; color:#95A5A6; margin-top:12px;\">Figures reflect the current filter and settings. Adjust the prior, credibility steepness, and seasonality toggle in the sidebar to test sensitivity. This summary is decision support, not a substitute for actuarial sign-off.<\/div>","final_headline":"<div style=\"display:flex; gap:14px; flex-wrap:wrap; margin-bottom:18px;\">\n  <div style=\"flex:1; min-width:200px; background:#fff; border-top:4px solid #B03A2E; border-radius:6px; padding:14px 16px; box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.08);\">\n    <div style=\"font-size:.8em; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.04em; color:#7F8C8D;\">Booked IBNR reserve<\/div>\n    <div style=\"font-size:1.6em; font-weight:700; color:#B03A2E;\">16,127,802<\/div>\n    <div style=\"font-size:.85em; color:#566573; margin-top:2px;\">Final post-adjustment figure<\/div>\n  <\/div>\n  <div style=\"flex:1; min-width:200px; background:#fff; border-top:4px solid #2C3E50; border-radius:6px; padding:14px 16px; box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.08);\">\n    <div style=\"font-size:.8em; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.04em; color:#7F8C8D;\">Model IBNR (selected bases)<\/div>\n    <div style=\"font-size:1.6em; font-weight:700; color:#2C3E50;\">14,278,512<\/div>\n    <div style=\"font-size:.85em; color:#566573; margin-top:2px;\">Pre-adjustment position<\/div>\n  <\/div>\n  <div style=\"flex:1; min-width:200px; background:#fff; border-top:4px solid #16A085; border-radius:6px; padding:14px 16px; box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.08);\">\n    <div style=\"font-size:.8em; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.04em; color:#7F8C8D;\">Judgemental overlay<\/div>\n    <div style=\"font-size:1.6em; font-weight:700; color:#16A085;\">+1,849,291<\/div>\n    <div style=\"font-size:.85em; color:#566573; margin-top:2px;\">5 origin period(s) adjusted<\/div>\n  <\/div>\n  <div style=\"flex:1; min-width:200px; background:#fff; border-top:4px solid #8E44AD; border-radius:6px; padding:14px 16px; box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.08);\">\n    <div style=\"font-size:.8em; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.04em; color:#7F8C8D;\">vs pure Chain Ladder<\/div>\n    <div style=\"font-size:1.6em; font-weight:700; color:#8E44AD;\">-9,408,916<\/div>\n    <div style=\"font-size:.85em; color:#566573; margin-top:2px;\">CL total: 25,536,718<\/div>\n  <\/div>\n<\/div>","guardrail":"<div class=\"alert alert-danger\">\n  <b>Selected ultimate below paid-to-date: <\/b>\n  2023-04-01\n  . This implies a negative reserve (net recoveries). Confirm this is intended before booking.\n<\/div>\n<div class=\"alert alert-warning\">\n  <b>Overrides without a rationale: <\/b>\n  2023-11-01\n  . Add a Comment so the audit log explains the judgement.\n<\/div>","exposure_status":"<div class=\"alert alert-secondary\">\n  <b>No exposure / earned premium loaded. <\/b>\n  Upload an .xlsx with columns Period, EarnedPremium, Exposure in the sidebar to switch the Bornhuetter-Ferguson, Benktander and Cape Cod methods onto a proper exposure base. Without it, those methods fall back to data-only (CL-seeded / equal-exposure) assumptions.\n<\/div>","recast_status":"<div class=\"alert alert-success\">Back-test complete: 20 held-back cells compared.<\/div>"},"value_boxes":{"vb_rows":"25,712","vb_total":"1,415,116,979","vb_span":"2021-01-01 -> 2023-12-31","vb_adj_base":"14,278,512","vb_adj_final":"16,127,802","vb_adj_delta":"+1,849,291","vb_exp_matched":"-","vb_exp_premium":"-","vb_exp_exposure":"-","cum_caption":"Cumulative triangle — C"},"mack":{"f":[2.3909148521190859,1.3570159008835807,1.1636875764938424,1.0889771425662675,1.0446233331619954